# Package-local ignores.
#
# This duplicates rules a surrounding repository almost certainly already has.
# That is the point: the package is shaped to be separated from whatever tree
# it currently sits in, and on the day it is copied out on its own it takes no
# root .gitignore with it. A bytecode cache is not merely clutter here - a
# .pyc embeds the ABSOLUTE SOURCE PATH it was compiled from, so a cache built
# in a private tree carries that tree's directory names inside a file that
# looks like a harmless build artifact.
#
# Plain ignore lines only. No `!` negation patterns: a negation whose parent
# directory is itself excluded never re-includes anything, so it reads as a
# deliberate exception while doing nothing at all.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
